WEBVTT

00:15.750 --> 00:18.590
I never dreamed before

00:18.590 --> 00:21.420
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.420 --> 00:24.990
into the world of perfect free

00:24.990 --> 00:27.100
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:27.100 --> 00:29.930
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.930 --> 00:32.670
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.670 --> 00:36.240
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.240 --> 00:37.410
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.410 --> 00:40.310
I was made to hit in America

00:40.310 --> 00:43.180
(I was made to hit in America)

00:43.180 --> 00:49.080
I was made to hit in America

00:49.080 --> 00:52.760
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.760 --> 00:54.760
(To me, forever)

00:54.760 --> 00:58.460
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.460 --> 01:01.690
(To me, forever)

01:08.540 --> 01:14.140
I was made to hit in America

01:14.140 --> 01:16.980
I was made to hit in America

01:16.980 --> 01:19.850
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.850 --> 01:22.650
I was made to hit in America

01:22.650 --> 01:25.420
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.420 --> 01:33.290
I was made to hit in America

01:37.500 --> 01:40.840
You're seriously thinking
about the revival of BECK,

01:40.840 --> 01:43.670
so I wondered if I could help.

01:43.670 --> 01:45.840
And what did Chiba-kun say?

01:45.840 --> 01:48.330
You will be dead!

01:50.010 --> 01:54.180
The conversation ended
in the worst way possible.

01:54.180 --> 01:55.520
It's so like Chiba-kun.

01:55.520 --> 01:58.520
-This is nothing to laugh at!
-Mmm.

01:58.520 --> 02:02.360
-Still...That ramen is bad!
-That ramen is bad!

02:02.360 --> 02:07.720
"Condor Ramen"

02:08.050 --> 02:09.390
Hello!

02:09.390 --> 02:11.720
-Hey...
-Chiba-kun, I...

02:11.720 --> 02:12.750
Were you the one who sent Maho?

02:12.750 --> 02:14.720
Were you the one who sent Maho?

02:14.720 --> 02:16.120
Huh...Err, no...

02:16.120 --> 02:19.420
Hah! Spouting her mouth off!

02:19.420 --> 02:21.360
What did Maho say?

02:21.360 --> 02:23.690
That there's no future
in bad-tasting ramen...

02:23.690 --> 02:26.760
so I should join up
with BECK when they regroup.

02:26.760 --> 02:29.930
That's all she kept saying.

02:29.930 --> 02:31.430
Chiba-kun!

02:31.430 --> 02:32.400
Huh?

02:33.100 --> 02:36.100
Let's revive BECK...one more time.

02:36.100 --> 02:37.370
Huh?

02:37.370 --> 02:41.880
Well...I'm the only one right now...

02:41.880 --> 02:46.440
Sorry, but right now...
I can only think about ramen.

02:53.990 --> 02:56.060
Hey, Koyuki!

02:56.060 --> 02:59.890
Is my ramen...that bad?

02:59.890 --> 03:01.400
Yeah...

03:01.400 --> 03:05.570
Are you serious about BECK?

03:05.570 --> 03:09.740
I have to be serious...
or there won't be another BECK!

03:09.740 --> 03:11.670
I can come back?

03:13.310 --> 03:15.740
I don't have to have a dream?

03:15.740 --> 03:18.750
What're you saying, Chiba-kun?!

03:18.750 --> 03:20.250
You're so late!

03:20.250 --> 03:23.920
I've been regretting it since
the day after Grateful Sound...

03:23.920 --> 03:26.750
Why'd that...

03:26.750 --> 03:28.090
Chiba-kun!

03:28.090 --> 03:31.260
But I can't make it up with Ryusuke!

03:31.260 --> 03:33.020
Chiba-kun...

04:18.410 --> 04:20.240
Taira-kun is awesome!

04:20.240 --> 04:22.080
That band was something else!

04:22.080 --> 04:24.850
Hurry it up before Taira leaves!

04:24.850 --> 04:27.580
Yeah...But if we're too hasty...

04:27.580 --> 04:28.750
Taira-kun!

04:28.750 --> 04:30.420
Hey, nice to see you.

04:30.420 --> 04:33.090
Taira...Yoshiaki's calling for you.

04:33.090 --> 04:34.690
Be right there.

04:34.690 --> 04:38.360
-Actually, I wanted to ask you
to return to BECK once...
-I got it.

04:38.360 --> 04:40.090
-Huh?
-You're regrouping BECK?

04:40.090 --> 04:41.100
Yes.

04:41.100 --> 04:44.870
I was planning to agree only
if you came to see me.

04:44.870 --> 04:47.200
-Taira-kun...
-Hey, hey...

04:47.200 --> 04:50.030
-Taira-kun!
-Idiot!

04:51.040 --> 04:54.880
I'm a member of Heroes now,
so I can't commit immediately.

04:54.880 --> 04:57.710
After the promotional tour,
I'll work it out with them.

04:57.710 --> 04:59.710
Taira-kun...

04:59.710 --> 05:01.980
However...I'm agreeing to return...

05:01.980 --> 05:05.720
...on the condition that all
five original members come back.

05:05.720 --> 05:06.890
Huh?!

05:06.890 --> 05:09.890
Otherwise, I want nothing
to do with this.

05:09.890 --> 05:11.390
Taira-kun...

05:11.390 --> 05:15.330
Sorry, but I'm busy. See ya.

05:17.060 --> 05:19.600
Well then, the big problem
here is Ryusuke.

05:19.600 --> 05:20.830
Yeah...

05:34.420 --> 05:38.350
Maybe...he's no longer in Japan.

05:39.690 --> 05:43.350
Even if he's away,
I think our spirit is one.

05:51.070 --> 05:52.530
"Saito Paper Company"

05:52.530 --> 05:55.640
"Saito Paper Company"

05:52.530 --> 05:55.640
Koyuki-kun, can you throw this out?

05:55.640 --> 05:57.040
"Saito Paper Company"

05:55.640 --> 05:57.040
Sure.

06:02.880 --> 06:06.210
Koyuki-kun, can you go shopping?

06:06.210 --> 06:08.550
I have a date with Momo-chan.

06:08.550 --> 06:09.980
All right.

06:14.460 --> 06:16.650
"Chinese Restaurant Sing Lung"

06:34.070 --> 06:35.240
I'm back.

06:35.240 --> 06:36.840
Oh, welcome home...

06:36.840 --> 06:38.350
Was there a phone call for me?

06:38.350 --> 06:40.510
No, there wasn't.

06:40.510 --> 06:41.670
I see.

07:42.340 --> 07:45.010
Man, that was a fantastic
live performance!

07:45.010 --> 07:48.350
If you told me you were coming,
I'd have put you down as guests.

07:48.350 --> 07:52.520
Taira-san, will you
take a picture with me?

07:52.520 --> 07:54.010
Sure.

07:55.690 --> 07:58.020
This is from Koyuki.

08:02.730 --> 08:04.370
Hey, Chiba!

08:04.370 --> 08:08.370
Don't keep your fan waiting,
you sexy rocker!

08:08.370 --> 08:09.630
Idiot!

08:11.710 --> 08:13.540
That Koyuki...

08:16.640 --> 08:20.310
There's a strange rumor
spreading among the fans.

08:20.310 --> 08:25.390
Yeah...Something about you
leaving Heroes after the tour.

08:25.390 --> 08:27.980
To rejoin BECK.

08:29.720 --> 08:31.460
I mean, geez...

08:31.460 --> 08:35.990
Why would anyone quit Heroes,
which is gonna sell 200,000 CDs?

08:37.160 --> 08:38.930
Hey, Taira!

08:39.500 --> 08:40.670
Wanna listen?

08:40.670 --> 08:41.340
-Huh?
-Huh?

08:41.340 --> 08:44.670
It's a rough cut.
But the genius shines through.

08:44.670 --> 08:48.380
I'm amazed he wrote so many songs.

08:48.380 --> 08:49.430
Huh?

08:50.340 --> 08:53.010
For everything up to now,
thank you so much!

08:53.010 --> 08:55.020
Think of me as a fool.

08:55.020 --> 08:57.150
But I'm going to return to BECK.

08:57.150 --> 08:58.850
-Are you kidding?!
-No shit?!

09:26.880 --> 09:28.820
Hey, Ryusuke Minami!

09:28.820 --> 09:31.890
Ho man, what a surprise!

09:31.890 --> 09:34.390
How long you been here
in New York?

09:34.390 --> 09:35.980
Mr. Davis...

09:44.830 --> 09:46.830
Okay, Ryusuke Minami...

09:46.830 --> 09:50.170
If I can help, I'll give you a hand.

09:51.170 --> 09:53.670
I really appreciate it, Mr. Davis.

09:53.670 --> 09:55.670
Doitashimashite. [You're welcome]

09:58.680 --> 10:01.520
Yukio! Phone call!

10:01.520 --> 10:02.850
Okay!

10:02.850 --> 10:04.180
Hello?

10:04.180 --> 10:06.350
Huh?! Yeah.

10:27.210 --> 10:29.710
Sorry to keep you waiting, Koyuki.

10:29.710 --> 10:32.550
-Saku!
-It took me a while
to save enough money.

10:32.550 --> 10:34.550
You're late!

10:34.550 --> 10:37.820
-Sorry.
-I was so worried!

10:37.820 --> 10:38.820
Koyuki...

10:38.820 --> 10:41.660
You haven't been
in touch lately, either.

10:41.660 --> 10:44.060
I wanted to come earlier...

10:44.060 --> 10:45.330
Saku...

10:45.330 --> 10:46.660
Koyuki...

10:47.900 --> 10:50.000
...just have to Stage Dive or Die

10:50.000 --> 10:52.000
Mind blower, a shower of sweat

10:52.000 --> 10:54.500
Run towards a new world, my life

10:54.500 --> 10:56.840
Those who seek it will be rewarded

10:56.840 --> 10:58.070
Pass the hot shot

10:58.070 --> 11:00.270
Keep on coming, come on!

11:00.270 --> 11:02.680
Blow your mind

11:02.680 --> 11:04.670
Squeeze your sweat yeah

11:06.410 --> 11:08.850
Your old man is stubborn.

11:09.580 --> 11:14.020
I couldn't convince him,
had'ta run away.

11:14.020 --> 11:15.020
Had'ta?

11:15.020 --> 11:19.030
You can stay at my house for as long
as it takes to find an apartment.

11:19.030 --> 11:20.530
I'm sa'happy.

11:20.530 --> 11:21.690
Sa'happy?

11:24.870 --> 11:29.200
Uh! Typhoon! Typhoon 24!

11:29.200 --> 11:30.870
24-7! Non-stop...

11:30.870 --> 11:33.710
Yukio, there's a phone call
from someone named Sato.

11:33.710 --> 11:34.700
All right!

11:35.710 --> 11:37.040
Hello?

11:37.040 --> 11:39.210
Congratulations on the revival of BECK!

11:39.210 --> 11:40.810
O-Oh, thank you.

11:40.810 --> 11:43.350
I'll get right to the point.

11:43.350 --> 11:44.150
Yes?

11:44.150 --> 11:48.060
There's an offer for BECK
for an American tour.

11:48.060 --> 11:49.390
America?

12:01.400 --> 12:02.240
Hello?

12:02.240 --> 12:03.330
Hey, what's up?

12:04.570 --> 12:06.510
I heard about you from John.

12:06.510 --> 12:07.740
I want to make a deal with you.

12:07.740 --> 12:11.750
I have a most valuable tape here
which I got from Eddy Lee.

12:11.750 --> 12:12.680
I'll give you this,

12:12.680 --> 12:16.750
instead I want you to leave
Mongolian Chop Squad alone forever.

12:16.750 --> 12:18.920
Right. Some deal...

12:18.920 --> 12:22.590
I'll bring the tape to
your hotel tonight anyway.

12:22.590 --> 12:25.020
You sure are a crazy dumb ass.

12:27.760 --> 12:28.860
If you never change

12:28.860 --> 12:33.360
I think there is no way my life fizzle out

12:36.270 --> 12:38.970
You open up the door with negative aura

12:38.970 --> 12:39.870
(I'm fed up fed up fed up)

12:39.870 --> 12:41.710
You say future is murky indeed...

12:41.710 --> 12:43.380
I'm sick of hearing gripe.

12:43.380 --> 12:45.880
An American tour?!

12:45.880 --> 12:47.210
That's unbelievable!

12:47.210 --> 12:48.880
Does that mean we
can throw television sets

12:48.880 --> 12:50.880
out the window like
Lead Zeppelin and the Stones...

12:50.880 --> 12:54.990
and fly around in groovy jets and stuff?

12:54.990 --> 13:00.550
Idiot! It's a hard tour...driving across
ten cities to perform in rock venues.

13:02.230 --> 13:05.070
-Ohh...
-Still, it's unbelievable.

13:05.070 --> 13:06.000
A band member of
a group called F.V.E.

13:06.000 --> 13:10.240
Saw us at Grateful Sound
and made the offer.

13:10.240 --> 13:13.070
-We've gotta do it!
-Think carefully!

13:13.070 --> 13:14.070
Huh?!

13:14.070 --> 13:18.010
Without Ryusuke...it's too risky
for BECK to do an American tour.

13:18.010 --> 13:18.750
But...

13:18.750 --> 13:21.980
It's not like us to turn down
a chance like this!

13:21.980 --> 13:23.420
But it's dangerous.

13:23.420 --> 13:24.590
America, huh...

13:24.590 --> 13:28.180
-We'd better get passports.
-Does that cost money?

13:29.020 --> 13:34.600
Summer vacation ended with BECK
rehearsals day in and day out.

13:34.600 --> 13:35.930
Man, look how dark you got!

13:35.930 --> 13:37.360
And you're so white!

13:37.360 --> 13:40.030
-Shaddup!
-Koyuki-kun, Saku-chan told me...

13:40.030 --> 13:42.370
But are you really
dropping out of school?

13:42.370 --> 13:43.200
Yeah.

13:44.040 --> 13:45.040
Koyuki-kun...

13:45.040 --> 13:47.710
I was hoping to
just fade out slowly...

13:47.710 --> 13:50.710
But with the American tour coming up,
I figured it's good timing.

13:50.710 --> 13:52.880
Aww...It'll be lonely without you guys.

13:52.880 --> 13:54.210
Sorry.

13:54.210 --> 13:55.720
America, huh?

13:55.720 --> 13:57.710
It's too far, I can't go.

14:01.390 --> 14:02.620
Farewell!

14:06.730 --> 14:09.900
This is an announcement
from the Student Council.

14:09.900 --> 14:12.570
On the 26th from 3pm...

14:12.570 --> 14:13.570
...my sister.

14:13.570 --> 14:14.740
...my sister.

14:13.570 --> 14:14.740
We began exhausting live performances
to prepare for the American Tour.

14:14.740 --> 14:17.340
In this world, which everyone is lonely.

14:14.740 --> 14:17.340
We began exhausting live performances
to prepare for the American Tour.

14:17.340 --> 14:19.410
In this world, which everyone is lonely.

14:19.410 --> 14:20.670
Yeah.

14:22.910 --> 14:24.910
If you are at a loss as to what to do.

14:24.910 --> 14:25.910
Raise you stiff middle finger.

14:25.910 --> 14:28.580
It will know which way the wind blows.

14:28.580 --> 14:31.590
Our last performance was at the Marquee.

14:31.590 --> 14:34.250
Our next live performance in town...

14:34.250 --> 14:36.260
None!

14:36.260 --> 14:43.030
Because BECK is starting a grueling 50-day,
46-city tour of the United States!

14:44.700 --> 14:47.360
-BECK is the best!
-Chiba!

14:53.210 --> 14:57.710
Uh! Typhoon! Typhoon 24!

14:57.710 --> 14:58.210
24-7! Non-stop...

14:58.210 --> 15:02.550
24-7! Non-stop...

14:58.210 --> 15:02.550
For this last live performance,
Chiba dove into the audience for the close.

15:02.550 --> 15:04.640
Man, that was painful! Yes.

15:06.920 --> 15:08.920
Huh? How was BECK?

15:08.920 --> 15:11.660
Your guitar was great.

15:11.660 --> 15:13.160
Really?

15:13.160 --> 15:14.330
Yeah.

15:14.330 --> 15:16.160
See ya.

15:16.160 --> 15:18.500
Koyuki, wasn't that...

15:18.500 --> 15:21.400
Hyodo. He was here as a guest.

15:21.400 --> 15:22.840
Is he in a band?

15:22.840 --> 15:26.740
They disbanded recently
and he's looking for new members.

15:26.740 --> 15:28.580
Oh...

15:28.580 --> 15:30.580
He said good luck
on our American Tour.

15:30.580 --> 15:32.340
Oh yeah?

15:35.420 --> 15:36.580
Don't kid yourself!

15:36.580 --> 15:38.190
I guess taking off for two months is...

15:38.190 --> 15:40.020
Damn right!

15:40.020 --> 15:41.520
Then I'll have to quit.

15:41.520 --> 15:44.690
It's easy to replace
someone like you!

15:44.690 --> 15:47.860
Thank you for everything.

15:47.860 --> 15:49.690
America, huh?

15:52.530 --> 15:54.840
Don't lose to the guys over there!

15:54.840 --> 15:56.370
Yes!

15:56.370 --> 15:57.600
Slip out of...

15:57.600 --> 15:59.770
Slip out ob.

15:59.770 --> 16:00.600
Out of!

16:01.440 --> 16:02.040
Out ob.

16:02.040 --> 16:04.040
You're hopeless!

16:04.040 --> 16:05.880
You leave tomorrow!

16:05.880 --> 16:08.320
If you can't pronounce
something like this,

16:08.320 --> 16:11.220
you'd better not go to America!

16:11.220 --> 16:13.390
Well Maho, you have
a hard time writing kanji.

16:13.390 --> 16:15.890
We're not talking about me!

16:15.890 --> 16:19.760
Can't you be a little more gentle?

16:19.760 --> 16:22.060
Well, excuse me
for not being gentle.

16:22.060 --> 16:23.400
You're so petty!

16:23.400 --> 16:25.990
You can drop dead
in America, Koyuki!

16:27.400 --> 16:29.340
Stupid Maho!

16:31.070 --> 16:34.910
This is Tanaka...I had reservations
for 2 at 7 o'clock.

16:34.910 --> 16:37.180
I'm sorry, but I have to cancel.

16:37.180 --> 16:38.350
Sorry.

16:38.350 --> 16:41.680
-Koyuki-kun, Maho forgot this.
-Huh?

16:41.680 --> 16:43.210
This is...

16:44.220 --> 16:46.190
"Lesson Cassette: 'Slip Out', For Koyuki"

16:46.190 --> 16:47.810
"Lesson Cassette: 'Slip Out', For Koyuki"

16:46.190 --> 16:47.810
Maho...

16:48.190 --> 16:50.520
What a fool

16:50.520 --> 16:54.190
I don't know 'bout tomorrow

16:54.190 --> 16:58.030
What it's like to be

17:01.540 --> 17:04.040
Yukio, do you have your passport?

17:04.040 --> 17:04.900
Yup.

17:05.870 --> 17:08.100
Then say goodbye to your father.

17:08.880 --> 17:09.670
All right.

17:14.880 --> 17:16.710
Did you call Grandma?

17:17.380 --> 17:18.480
Yup.

17:23.560 --> 17:27.060
No matter how many times
I look at it, it's a rough schedule.

17:27.060 --> 17:29.400
Are we really gonna
make it in 50 days?

17:29.400 --> 17:31.990
What will be will be!
That's all there is to know!

17:38.170 --> 17:40.540
Umm...Is this it?

17:41.680 --> 17:43.870
Hey, it's so blurred!

17:44.850 --> 17:47.180
All right, there's the American continent!

17:47.180 --> 17:49.340
-Is that the wing of the jet?
-Uh-huh.

17:50.350 --> 17:55.020
David Eric of the popular
F.V.E. Band came to pick us up.

17:55.020 --> 17:56.510
He's out of focus.

17:57.520 --> 18:00.860
-This is an alien base.
-No, it's the L.A. Airport.

18:00.860 --> 18:03.700
-Our hotel.
-Hey, pretty nice!

18:03.700 --> 18:05.870
This was the only nice hotel.

18:05.870 --> 18:09.700
-Umm...Chiba-kun studying.
-Some study.

18:09.700 --> 18:14.370
-We performed live here.
-It says Mongolian Chop Squad!

18:14.370 --> 18:16.210
But we just couldn't get it together.

18:16.210 --> 18:18.880
-The audience is looking down.
-Chiba is depressed.

18:18.880 --> 18:20.400
Put it on spin!

18:21.380 --> 18:25.720
-These are members of other bands.
-Where are you, Koyuki?

18:25.720 --> 18:30.060
-We traveled in this car.
-Saku's practically kissing the windshield!

18:30.060 --> 18:33.230
-Hey, lots of people!
-We're not performing.

18:33.230 --> 18:35.900
-Look at the color of her hair!
-The Lizards. That's a guy.

18:35.900 --> 18:37.460
Huh!?

18:37.460 --> 18:40.030
We sold our CDs.
We sold quite a bit actually.

18:40.030 --> 18:41.500
Hmm...

18:41.500 --> 18:45.010
-This is the car we traveled in.
-Looks so American.

18:45.010 --> 18:47.500
-We're frogs.
-Silly!

18:48.380 --> 18:51.010
-This is the car...
-I get it already!

18:51.010 --> 18:52.850
Hey, are they clowns?

18:52.850 --> 18:55.850
-This live was great.
-But I can't see you.

18:55.850 --> 18:59.350
It was great! Hurrah for Long Beach!

18:59.350 --> 19:02.020
-We had a session together.
-What're you doing, Koyuki?

19:02.020 --> 19:04.020
-Oh, you had a flat tire.
-Yes.

19:04.020 --> 19:05.620
That's Chiba-kun.

19:06.690 --> 19:09.860
-Look at the clouds!
-It's more awesome when
you actually see them.

19:09.860 --> 19:11.200
Hmm...

19:11.200 --> 19:15.040
-Oh, another session?
-Taira-kun was popular even in America.

19:15.040 --> 19:17.370
-And here's Chiba-kun.
-Koyuki, you look so cute.

19:17.370 --> 19:20.040
We were near total exhaustion.

19:20.040 --> 19:23.040
-Looks like fun.
-A short moment of relaxation.

19:23.040 --> 19:27.050
-Here we are in New York!
-This picture's so dark!

19:27.050 --> 19:29.480
-Taking a stroll in New York.
-Did you eat hot dogs?

19:29.480 --> 19:30.720
Yup!

19:30.720 --> 19:34.050
This is CBGB.
The audience is to the right.

19:34.050 --> 19:37.460
-And this is...
-That's the man...New York Punk.

19:38.460 --> 19:39.760
Who is he?

19:39.760 --> 19:43.830
He's Kevin Eric. The guitarist
and leader of F.V.E.

19:43.830 --> 19:46.330
-He's David's older brother.
-Hmm...

19:46.330 --> 19:50.170
-It's blurred again!
-Well, Kevin's a scary guy.

19:50.170 --> 19:52.510
-And this guy...
-Yup, that's...

19:52.510 --> 19:54.010
Umm...Texas, I think.

19:54.010 --> 19:56.340
-We even traveled
through a place like this.
-Hmm...

19:56.340 --> 20:00.180
-Golden Gate Bridge.
-That's San Francisco!

20:00.180 --> 20:02.340
-And this is...
-Seattle.

20:03.350 --> 20:05.050
And that's Pike Place Market.

20:05.050 --> 20:06.680
-A supermarket?
-You can see fish jumping.

20:07.690 --> 20:08.850
And the Space Needle.

20:09.860 --> 20:11.360
And Jimi Hendrix.

20:11.360 --> 20:13.190
Chiba-kun had a dream.

20:13.190 --> 20:15.030
And he heard Jimi say,
"Let's meet at my grave."

20:15.030 --> 20:18.700
-Grave?
-And the day was September 18.

20:18.700 --> 20:24.040
-The day mentioned in Ryusuke's message.
-And also, the day Jimi Hendrix died.

20:24.040 --> 20:26.030
Koyuki, you're cut off.

20:27.040 --> 20:30.040
-This is Jimi Hendrix's grave.
-Hmm...

20:30.040 --> 20:33.050
And...we found Ryusuke.

20:33.050 --> 20:35.050
Beck and Keith, too?

20:35.050 --> 20:36.380
Yep.

20:37.380 --> 20:39.320
It's blurred again.

20:40.750 --> 20:42.960
Oh, this is the newspaper article.

20:42.960 --> 20:47.160
-So Leon was arrested.
-And Ryusuke was right there.

20:47.160 --> 20:50.000
I'm so glad he's alive!

20:50.000 --> 20:52.330
-Oh, you saw this already.
-Yeah.

20:54.070 --> 20:58.170
And...we met up with Ryusuke,
who had Lucille,

20:58.170 --> 21:01.340
at the Crocodile Cafe in Seattle.

21:01.340 --> 21:05.010
It was the first time all five members
were together since coming to America.

21:05.010 --> 21:06.340
Now this is BECK!

21:07.350 --> 21:10.340
-Koyuki, let's do "Slip Out."
-Right.

21:44.050 --> 21:50.560
I don't know since when I changed
to such a cold-hearted guy.

21:50.560 --> 21:56.730
I have to warm this frozen icy
lonely heart to thaw.

21:56.730 --> 22:02.740
I like being wrapped with warmness
more than anything else for sure.

22:02.740 --> 22:11.410
I'm gonna make my coming days
to be filled with laughter and joy

22:12.750 --> 22:15.080
Hey, what're you doing?!

22:15.080 --> 22:16.750
I let myself down that I'm more cruel
then I thought I would be.

22:15.080 --> 22:16.750
Stop teasing him!

22:16.750 --> 22:19.740
I let myself down that I'm more cruel
then I thought I would be.

22:16.750 --> 22:19.740
Shut up! Let's go, everyone!

22:23.260 --> 22:25.430
Beck! Come here!

22:25.430 --> 22:28.090
I told you,
you shouldn't go out alone.

22:28.090 --> 22:29.100
You...

22:29.100 --> 22:31.030
You made me worry.

22:31.030 --> 22:33.760
A foreigner?

22:35.940 --> 22:38.200
Isn't this dog ugly?

22:38.200 --> 22:42.230
Thank you for saving Beck.

22:40.030 --> 22:45.000
Sorrow isn't what I am,
but its growing my sensation

22:46.070 --> 22:52.240
Regrets taught me how
to make any hard decisions.

22:52.240 --> 22:58.580
Peace is always by my side
but I've never felt it once.

22:58.580 --> 23:05.590
Love is not the word only
for the sweet romance. Yeah.

23:05.590 --> 23:11.760
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

23:11.760 --> 23:18.100
And I'm scared to keep on
going on my way. Yeah.

23:18.100 --> 23:24.280
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

23:24.280 --> 23:29.870
And I tell myself
I'm special till the end.

23:46.400 --> 23:52.900
I don't give my heart to no one
cause I don't wanna waste my time.

23:52.900 --> 24:01.000
I tried to love this loneliness
to slip out of lonesome hole.
